1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:00,730
Hello!

2
00:00:00,730 --> 00:00:05,820
This week you will learn to follow a discussion in Listening Section 3,

3
00:00:05,820 --> 00:00:11,484
a lecture in Section 4, and to speak for nearly two minutes in Speaking Part 2.

4
00:00:12,784 --> 00:00:13,562
Point one:

5
00:00:13,562 --> 00:00:14,340
Section 3.

6
00:00:14,340 --> 00:00:16,284
Two to four people speak.

7
00:00:16,284 --> 00:00:19,784
Remember the names and voices from the start,

8
00:00:19,784 --> 00:00:25,384
and notice whether each speaker agrees or disagrees with the one before.

9
00:00:26,684 --> 00:00:30,428
I see what you mean, but I'm not sure that would work.

10
00:00:33,728 --> 00:00:34,842
Exactly.

11
00:00:34,842 --> 00:00:37,904
That's my concern too.

12
00:00:40,704 --> 00:00:41,347
Point two:

13
00:00:41,347 --> 00:00:47,002
Section 4 is a lecture, usually with note completion that follows the order of the talk.

14
00:00:47,002 --> 00:00:52,272
Stay with the signposting, which are the words that guide you through the lecture.

15
00:00:53,572 --> 00:00:56,125
Moving on to the benefits.

16
00:00:56,125 --> 00:00:58,972
However, there are drawbacks.

17
00:01:02,272 --> 00:01:05,209
Answers in Section 4 are often nouns.

18
00:01:05,209 --> 00:01:08,147
Check your spelling and the plural s.

19
00:01:08,147 --> 00:01:14,815
Also, the questions often paraphrase what the lecturer says, so listen for the idea,

20
00:01:14,815 --> 00:01:16,720
not for identical words.

21
00:01:18,020 --> 00:01:19,042
Point three:

22
00:01:19,042 --> 00:01:19,638
Part 2.

23
00:01:19,638 --> 00:01:22,277
You have one minute to prepare.

24
00:01:22,277 --> 00:01:26,450
Write only five to eight keywords, not sentences.

25
00:01:26,450 --> 00:01:29,685
When you speak, follow this framework:

26
00:01:29,685 --> 00:01:34,028
opening, background, highlight, reason, and ending.

27
00:01:35,328 --> 00:01:39,288
I'd like to talk about a teacher who changed how I study.

28
00:01:42,588 --> 00:01:47,220
What I remember most is the day I finally understood fractions.

29
00:01:50,520 --> 00:01:53,761
Looking back, I'm glad I didn't give up.

30
00:01:53,761 --> 00:01:57,408
It made me realise how much patience matters.

31
00:02:00,708 --> 00:02:01,870
Common mistakes.

32
00:02:01,870 --> 00:02:08,116
In Section 3, choosing the first speaker's idea even after the next speaker disagrees.

33
00:02:08,116 --> 00:02:13,128
In Section 4, getting lost when the lecturer moves on to a new point.

34
00:02:13,128 --> 00:02:18,067
In Part 2, writing full sentences during the one-minute preparation,

35
00:02:18,067 --> 00:02:21,553
or speaking for forty seconds and then stopping,

36
00:02:21,553 --> 00:02:25,620
or mixing the present tense into a story about the past.

37
00:02:27,420 --> 00:02:28,066
Quiz one:

38
00:02:28,066 --> 00:02:31,077
the phrase on the other hand signals what:

39
00:02:31,077 --> 00:02:33,946
an example, a contrast, or a conclusion?

40
00:02:33,946 --> 00:02:34,591
Quiz two:

41
00:02:34,591 --> 00:02:39,181
when the lecturer says let's turn to, what is the lecture doing?

42
00:02:39,181 --> 00:02:39,970
Quiz three:

43
00:02:39,970 --> 00:02:45,348
in the one-minute preparation, should you write full sentences or keywords?

44
00:02:49,648 --> 00:02:50,323
Answers.

45
00:02:50,323 --> 00:02:50,661
One:

46
00:02:50,661 --> 00:02:54,963
a contrast, which means an opposite idea is coming.

47
00:02:54,963 --> 00:02:55,301
Two:

48
00:02:55,301 --> 00:02:57,579
moving on to a new section.

49
00:02:57,579 --> 00:02:58,085
Three:

50
00:02:58,085 --> 00:03:05,172
keywords, because writing full sentences makes you read them out instead of speaking

51
00:03:05,172 --> 00:03:06,016
naturally.

52
00:03:08,316 --> 00:03:08,860
Summary:

53
00:03:08,860 --> 00:03:14,031
listen for who agrees and who disagrees, follow the signposting in lectures,

54
00:03:14,031 --> 00:03:16,888
and use the five-step framework in Part 2.

55
00:03:16,888 --> 00:03:22,535
Do the week seven exercises in the app, record yourself on your phone, listen back,

56
00:03:22,535 --> 00:03:25,188
and tick the self-assessment checklist.
